                "id": "bennu-surface",
                "path": "../manifest.json"
              },
              "falseColor": false,
              "notes": "The 5 cm global image basemap retains surface texture and photographed shading. It was normalized to 30° phase and registered to the SPC v28 control shape; small differences from the OLA v20 display mesh remain. This is a separate observed image view; it does not silently fill the albedo view’s missing poles."
            },
            {
              "id": "spectral",
              "label": "Spectral color",
              "thumbnail": "/scenes/bennu/bennu-spectral-thumbnail.webp",
              "surface": "bennu-spectral-surface@2x.webp",
              "poles": "bennu-spectral-surface@2x.webp",
              "source": {
                "id": "bennu-spectral",
                "path": "../manifest.json"
              },
              "falseColor": true,
              "notes": "Published MapCam false-color composite over 550 nm normal reflectance. Red shows the 847/550 nm ratio, green the 698 nm band strength, and blue the 473/550 nm ratio. These colors show spectral differences, not natural color or mineral abundance. Coverage extends to about 65° north and south; omitted shadows and gaps use the gray grid. The controlled map is draped on the simplified OLA shape, so individual boulders need not align precisely.",
              "noData": true
            },
